  "tier": "told-once",
  "plain": "In the 1960s the rocket engineer Wernher von Braun, talking about Moon facts in Time magazine, is said to have given a figure for the neutral gravity point, the spot between Earth and Moon where their pulls cancel out, that was about double the officially stated distance. The comedian Kurt Metzger repeats this from the author Joseph P. Farrell, as a hint that what the public was told about the Moon may not match what the experts knew."
